Kind: ablation
Issue: #963
Takes out: what the HAL may hand on: the AHCI class instead of any function (#964).  A chora holds what its parent hands on, cut by exec_server to the parent's delegatable lines: the HAL's chora on the card holds no function, cap_server refuses it the card's, and it never claims it -- its authority is its parent's to give.
Run: --iommu intel --entry 68 600 -smp 4
Expect: @[0-9a-f]{2}:[0-9a-f]{2}\.[0-7]: no capability for function [0-9a-f]{2}:[0-9a-f]{2}\.[0-7]: cap_request 0x
Expect: chora_test: \[2\] WRONG -- the HAL.s chora on the card, and 30 s on the kernel says nobody claims it
Note: made again over #964, where the HAL starts the chora on the card and writes its manifest; it took chora_test's own line before, when chora_test started it.

diff --git a/uros/src/servers/hal_server/hal_server.manifest b/uros/src/servers/hal_server/hal_server.manifest
index 6818dfbf..180beb88 100644
--- a/uros/src/servers/hal_server/hal_server.manifest
+++ b/uros/src/servers/hal_server/hal_server.manifest
@@ -31,4 +31,4 @@ required 5 any 0x7
 # into the chora's manifest, at run time, the one function's address (#982).
 # exec_server cuts that manifest to this line.  `any' because no manifest
 # names an address.
-delegatable 12 any 0x7
+delegatable 5 0x010601 0x7
